But I also found the **real bug**: `tsort_range((uint64_t)e<<20, ...)` compares `(tsort[m]>>20)` (the unshifted tgt) against `e<<20` — an off-by-20-bits comparison that makes every lookup return an empty range, so the candidate resolution process was never being executed. Let me rewrite it with the fixes applied:

